lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120432","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120432","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120432.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120432.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Up to 4.6.3-stable, an exported float property with NaN as default value is displayed as 0.0 with revert button activated. The display issue is already addressed in commit `7d30a7b495e`. However, the revert button issue remains unresolved. This PR adds a simple patch in `PropertyUtils::is_property_value_different`.\r\n\r\n`PropertyUtils::is_property_value_different` appears to be the appropriate place. It compares a current value against a baseline value. Therefore, considering NaN equal to itself is expected. This does not change normal IEEE-754 or Variant equality semantics.\r\n\r\nRelated issue: #50715 \r\n\r\nbefore/after:\r\n<img width=\"931\" height=\"720\" alt=\"comparison\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9dd05d48-bf1d-4152-a053-16c67bf5d93f\" />","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120432/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120432/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}